#### problem

The new model-to-data Challenge workflow does not currently have logic in place to return Docker execution logs to participants and/or organizers after a Docker container run is complete. These execution logs should display any warning, error, or general standard output messages received as a result of the execution of the Docker container, in order to provide insight for troubleshooting and/or model improvements.

#### solution

The solution proposed in this PR is to upload a `[submission-id]_docker.log` file to the `Logs/` root folder under the subfolder `[submitter-id]/docker_logs`. Each submission will only have 1 `[submission-id]_docker.log` file. The log file have the same name whether or not it contains an error message.

```
Logs
 ├── 3123456
 │  ├── docker_logs
 │  │  ├── 9123456_docker.log
 │ ...
 │
 ├── 3123455
 │ ...
 │
...
```
The largest structural change to the workflow is the new `run_docker.py` script which wraps the Docker python SDK to run the Docker container submission and generate the relevant log/predictions file + upload them into Synapse. As a result of this, `UPDATE_FOLDERS.nf` is done away with, and `create_folders.py` is modified and generalized to accomodate the upload of logfiles to Synapse. This new structural change updates the workflow like so:

```mermaid
flowchart LR;
    A[SYNAPSE STAGE]-->E[RUN DOCKER];
    B[UPDATE STATUS]-->E;
    C[CREATE FOLDERS]-->E;
    E-->G[UPDATE STATUS];
    G-->H[VALIDATE];
    H-->I[ANNOTATE];
    H-->J[UPDATE STATUS];
    I-->K[SCORE];
    J-->K;
    K-->L[ANNOTATE];
    K-->M[UPDATE STATUS];
    L-->N;
    M-->N[SEND EMAIL];
N-->O[END];
```

- [x] Add a new python script (`run_docker.py`) using the Docker python SDK to generate a logfile and upload it and the predictions file(s) onto Synapse
- [x] Modify `RUN_DOCKER.nf` to write stdout/stderr to a log file and create a new output channel for that file
- [x] Modify `MODEL_TO_DATA.nf` to reflect the new `RUN_DOCKER.nf` log file output channel
- [x] Remove `UPDATE_FOLDERS.nf`
- [x] Modify `create_folders.py` to take the input log file and upload it into Synapse
- [x] Refactor where appropriate
- [x] Reformat the `stderr` to make it readable
- [x] Update documentation where appropriate

